From 62a2940252c971675b80731b0112bd8774d53bd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:28:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drv_helpers: Do not pad one-row dumb buffers

drv_dumb_bo_create_ex() aligns width and height to the llvmpipe tile size
of 64. A BLOB buffer (HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_BLOB, R8) is a single row as long
as its size in bytes:

- The height alignment made it 64 times as large: the 7.5 MB JPEG
  buffer of a 5 MP camera still became a 477 MB dumb buffer and
  DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB failed with ENOMEM on every capture.
- The width alignment moves the end of the plane by up to 63 bytes. The
  camera HAL writes the JPEG size (camera3_jpeg_blob) at the end of the
  plane, the framework reads it at the end of the requested width, so
  apps saved the whole 7.5 MB buffer instead of the 1.3 MB JPEG.

Leave one-row buffers unpadded.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Change-Id: I2359be4f71076e33e52ec22c6df6d0d5364f2029
---
 drv_helpers.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drv_helpers.c b/drv_helpers.c
index 47c78b4..09f3096 100644
--- a/drv_helpers.c
+++ b/drv_helpers.c
@@ -394,9 +394,18 @@ int drv_dumb_bo_create_ex(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32
 		    DIV_ROUND_UP(aligned_width * layout_from_format(format)->bytes_per_pixel[0], 4);
 		create_dumb.bpp = 32;
 	} else {
-		/* Align for llvmpipe 64-byte tile size for dumb_driver */
-		aligned_width = ALIGN(aligned_width, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
-		aligned_height = ALIGN(aligned_height, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
+		/*
+		 * Align for llvmpipe 64-byte tile size for dumb_driver, but not
+		 * a single row: BLOB buffers (JPEG) are one row of their size
+		 * in bytes. 64 rows made the 7.5 MB JPEG buffer of 5 MP stills
+		 * a 477 MB allocation that always failed, and a padded row
+		 * moves the end of the buffer, where the camera HAL puts the
+		 * JPEG size, away from where the framework looks for it.
+		 */
+		if (aligned_height > 1) {
+			aligned_width = ALIGN(aligned_width, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
+			aligned_height = ALIGN(aligned_height, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
+		}
 		create_dumb.bpp = layout_from_format(format)->bytes_per_pixel[0] * 8;
 	}
 	create_dumb.width = aligned_width;
